name: getent --help after a database; the bug-report lines are identity strings (D-31.4)
clause: s31_1_c_2
command: getent
namespace: user
# A private /etc: nsswitch.conf names only the files service, so nothing depends on the host's
# configuration, network or name servers.
dir: etc
bind: etc /etc
file: etc/nsswitch.conf
| passwd: files
| group: files
| shadow: files
| gshadow: files
| hosts: files
| networks: files
| protocols: files
| services: files
| ethers: files
| rpc: files
| netgroup: files
| aliases: files
# The reference's bug-report lines are an identity string (D-31.4): libniji prints none.
normalise: shadow\n\nFor bug reporting instructions, please see:\n<https://bugs.launchpad.net/ubuntu/+source/glibc/+bugs>.\n => shadow\n
arg: passwd
arg: --help
status: exit 0
stdout:
| Usage: getent [OPTION...] database [key ...]
| Get entries from administrative database.
|
| \x20 -A, --no-addrconfig        do not filter out unsupported IPv4/IPv6 addresses
| \x20                            (with ahosts*)
| \x20 -i, --no-idn               disable IDN encoding
| \x20 -s, --service=CONFIG       Service configuration to be used
| \x20 -?, --help                 Give this help list
| \x20     --usage                Give a short usage message
| \x20 -V, --version              Print program version
|
| Mandatory or optional arguments to long options are also mandatory or optional
| for any corresponding short options.
|
| Supported databases:
| ahosts ahostsv4 ahostsv6 aliases ethers group gshadow hosts initgroups
| netgroup networks passwd protocols rpc services shadow
stderr:
